            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0585" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-15T15:00:00+07:00">September 15,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 15—10:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1558. Wu Teh-chen, Secretary General [of] Kuomintang, informs us People’s
                    Political Council is to be reconstituted hereafter by increasing number of
                    delegates from 240 to 290 to be elected by provincial, city and district
                    councils and is to be given right to investigate and examine national
                    budget.</p>
                <p>It is understood Kmt–CCP negotiations are to be discussed in today’s session. In
                    a telegram from Yenan of September 11 Service reported Communist representatives
                    to PPC have been instructed to propose summoning of conference of all political
                    groups for creation of a national government.</p>
                <p>First week of session was devoted largely to presentation of government reports
                    and interpellations of delegates many of which were sharply critical and this
                    week delegates deliberating 200 proposals presented for consideration. Session
                    scheduled to close 19th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
